## Platform context (do not ask about these)

- **MCU**: ATmega32U4 (8-bit AVR) @ 16 MHz, 32 KB flash (28 KB usable after Caterina bootloader), 2.5 KB RAM, 1 KB internal EEPROM.
- **Board**: Custom `N32B` and `N32Bv3` (Leonardo variant).
- **Framework**: Arduino (`atmelavr` platform), PlatformIO, `-Os`.
- **Architecture**: Bare-metal superloop (`setup()` / `loop()`). Not FreeRTOS, not a cooperative scheduler.
- **Storage**: Internal EEPROM (1 KB) via `<EEPROM.h>`. Byte-level read/write with `EEPROM.read()` / `EEPROM.update()`.

## Peripherals in use

| Bus | Usage |
|-----|-------|
| Bit-bang SPI | N32B: MAX7219 7-segment LED display (`DigitLedDisplay`, pins DIN/CS/CLK) |
| Bit-bang SPI | N32Bv3: TLC59282 7-segment LED display (`TLC59282_Display`, pins SIN/SCLK/LAT/BLANK) |
| UART | MIDI Serial x1 (`MIDISerial1` on `Serial1`) |
| USB | USB-MIDI (`USB-MIDI` library), native USB on ATmega32U4 |
| ADC | 32 analog inputs (knobs/pots) via 2x 16-channel analog multiplexers, polled with `analogRead()` |
| GPIO | 2 buttons (A3, A2, INPUT_PULLUP), 1 LED (pin 17), 4 mux select lines |

No I2C. No CAN. No external EEPROM.

## ADC subsystem

- Polled in the main loop: `ADC_MUX::update()` iterates all 32 inputs sequentially each `loop()` cycle.
- `analogRead()` with 50 µs mux settling delay per channel.
- 10-bit native resolution, scaled to 14-bit domain (0–16383) for MIDI processing (NRPN/RPN/14-bit modes).
- Fixed-point exponential moving average (EMA) filter.
- Idle/in-motion state machine per pot with configurable thresholds and release counter.

## Real-time constraints

- All ADC reads and MIDI sends happen in the main loop — no ISR-based ADC on this platform.
- MIDI reading is polled (`doMidiRead()`), not timer-driven.
- Display updates happen in the main loop — soft deadline.
- 32 × `analogRead()` + mux settling dominates loop time (~5–6 ms per full scan).

## Timing

- No hardware cycle counter on ATmega32U4.
- `millis()` wraps at ~49.7 days — rarely an issue but be aware.
- `micros()` resolution is 4 µs on 16 MHz AVR.
- Use `millis()` for elapsed-time measurements; handle wraparound via unsigned subtraction.

## Memory constraints

- **2.5 KB RAM** — extremely tight. `Preset_t` is ~289 bytes; `Device_t` with 32 `Pot` objects is a significant portion of RAM.
- `ArduinoSTL` provides `<vector>` and `<bitset>` — used sparingly, beware heap fragmentation.
- `PROGMEM` for constant data (`firmwareVersion`, `knobsLocation`). Use `pgm_read_*` to access.
- EEPROM layout: byte 0 = last used preset, then `NUMBER_OF_PRESETS` × `sizeof(Preset_t)` contiguous, firmware signature at end.

## Arduino-specific anti-patterns

- **`delay()` / `delayMicroseconds()`**: Acceptable only during one-time init sequences. Never in the main loop (except the 50 µs mux settle and N32Bv3 display timing which are established patterns).
- **`digitalRead()` / `digitalWrite()`**: Used for mux select lines and buttons — acceptable given the polling architecture.
- **`String` class**: Never use. Use C-style char arrays.
- **Dynamic allocation**: Minimize. The ArduinoSTL `vector` usage should not grow at runtime.

## Board variants

- `N32B` — Original board. MAX7219 display driver (`DigitLedDisplay`). Mux select on pins 2–5. Non-sequential knob-to-index mapping via `knobsLocation[]` PROGMEM table.
- `N32Bv3` — V3 board (`-DN32Bv3` build flag). TLC59282 display driver (`TLC59282_Display`). Mux select on pins 4–7. Sequential knob indexing. Additional display pins (BLANK).

## Build environments

- `N32B` — Original board build (default).
- `N32Bv3` — V3 board build (`-DN32Bv3`).

## Libraries

- `ArduinoSTL` — STL containers for AVR.
- `USB-MIDI` — USB MIDI transport (lathoub).
- `DigitLedDisplay` — MAX7219 driver (N32B only).
- `TLC59282_Display` — Custom TLC59282 driver in `lib/` (N32Bv3 only).
- `ezButton` — Button debouncing.
